language 0.1.0
module source
  means
    Text taken as the subject of processing: the characters it is made of,
    the coordinates by which a place in it is named, and the way those
    characters are represented.

entity source-text : thing
  means
    source text: a body of characters processed as a whole and read from a
    single origin.

entity character : thing
  means
    character: the smallest unit of a source text, indivisible for the
    purpose of processing.

entity line : thing
  means
    line: the characters of a source text between two line breaks, taken in
    their order.

entity position : thing
  means
    position: a place in a source text, named by the line and the offset
    within it.

entity span : thing
  means
    span: a continuous stretch of a source text between two positions.

entity excerpt : thing
  means
    excerpt: the characters of a span, reproduced apart from the source text
    they belong to.

entity encoding : thing
  means
    encoding: a correspondence between characters and the bytes representing
    them.

entity whitespace : thing
  means
    whitespace: a character separating others and carrying no meaning beyond
    the separation.
